mod:store_through_pointer_value_walks;
// Landing 177d2b6, row 4 (V+D with form (h)), the second file: what form (h)'s walks refuse beside V+D (store_through_pointer_value.npk holds what V+D
// refuses alone: a callee's store through a pointer VALUE, carried to what it points at, one level below the place the argument names, the argument
// walked as written). Form (h) keeps `rrti_held`'s reading and adds the name road's beside it, at the value's own pointer type, and walks a pointer to a
// pointer on into its target's chain (rule A's depth arm) and a pointer's name under casts at BOTH types, as written and under the casts, each walk on
// its own pairs and fuel. One site per face closed here, each a fault on main (8a2b40b) and on row 3's text (7ebd69c):
//   DEF-643's four store faces (`c1c2ter`, `c2t2bang`, `c2t2opt`, `c2t2pick`) and DEF-644's `t_fld`;
//   a pointee-changing cast on V's value road: in the argument (`a_pcn`, `a_pcn2`, `a_pcnm`, `a_pcnw`), in the holder's initializer (`a_pcni`, `a_pcni2`,
//   `a_pcnim`) or in the callee's body (`a_pcc`, `a_pcc2`, `a_pccm`), and a parameter's value (`m_pck`); a pointer to a pointer (`a_pp`, `a_ppp`, `a_ppt`,
//   `a_ppa`);
//   (u)'s walk beside `rrti_held`: `c_d4`, `c_d4t`, `c_gencg` (Addendum 25's `c_gen`, renamed in this suite), `c_ra3`, `c_rac`, `c_raq`, `c_retyi`,
//   `h_rcc`, `h_rccp`, `h_rapcp`; its rule A depth arm over the whole holder (`p_uraf`, `p_ura2f`, `f_re`, `f_nest`, `f_whole`), and at the target's own
//   type where a cast retyped it (`h_rapc`, `h_rapcc`, `h_rapci`, `h_rapa`, `h_rapcca`, `h_rapcia`, `h_d5r`, `h_rany`, `h_rsa`);
//   both types: a middle pointer stored at its written type (`h_mix`, `h_mixp`, `h_mx4`, `h_mx4r`, `h_mxg`, `h_mxl`, `h_mxlr`, `pp_onf`, `pp_onrf`,
//   `pp_kpf`, `pp_kprf`), and depth five under casts (`h_d5t`, `h_d5m`, `h_d5mr`, `h_d5ri`);
//   a pointer read out of a by-value parameter's pointer field (`sp.qq`, `pa[0]`, `so.oqq`, `sr.rq`), cast (`q8_ac`, `q8_awc`, `q8_ofc`, `q8_rfc`,
//   `q8_sc`, `q8_swc`) and plain (`q8_ap`, `q8_ofp`, `q8_rfp`, `q8_sp`, `q8_awp`, `q8_swp`);
//   row 4's (h) attack's: the mark at the top of a chain, r = 0 (`y20p`, `y20h`, `y20l`; `w10p`, `w10r` at depth 10; `z50q`, `z50k`, `z50c`, `z50i`;
//   `z5khp` under a cast of a cast), rule A's at r = 1 and r = D-1 (`y51r`, `y54r`, `z51q`, `z51k`, `z51c`, `z51i`, `z54q`, `z54k`, `z54c`, `z54i`),
//   and its sensitivity fault `pz_3f` (`a_pp`'s family).
// Each cell's declarations carry its name as a suffix, and its `main` is `cell_main_<name>`. The controls that run are in
// tests/backend/programs/store_through_pointer_value_ok.npk.
// PRICES: the cells marked PRICE below are right programs this row's text refuses, each failing closed; each comment names its by-name twin. At parity
// (form (h)'s, the twin refused on every build) or not at parity (DEF-655's, the twin running in the _ok file).
error:E5;
struct:K_a_pcn = { int64:k; };
struct:H_a_pcn = { List<int64>:l; int64:k; K_a_pcn:kk; };
func:mk_a_pcn = List<int64>() never fails { List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(1i64); drop list_push(@l, 1i64); pass l; };
func:mkh_a_pcn = H_a_pcn() never fails { pass H_a_pcn{ l: raw mk_a_pcn(), k: 2i64, kk: K_a_pcn{ k: 3i64 } }; };
func:growh_a_pcn = int64(H_a_pcn->:w) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(@w.l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:growl_a_pcn = int64(List<int64>->:l) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:fp_a_pcn = int64->(H_a_pcn->:q) never fails { pass @((<-q).l[0i64]); };
func:idh_a_pcn = H_a_pcn->(H_a_pcn->:q) never fails { pass q; };
func:getl_a_pcn = List<int64>->(H_a_pcn->:w) never fails { pass @w.l; };
